How to Ace Your R2 Technical Interview for Cloud, DevOps, SRE, Platform & AI/ML Ops Roles?


Round 2 interviews aren’t just about theory—they test your ability to think, design, and troubleshoot like a pro. Here’s a roadmap to make yourself competent and confident for these roles:
✅ 1. Decode the Role
Each role has unique priorities:
Cloud Engineer: Multi-region architecture, IAM, cost optimization.
DevOps: CI/CD pipelines, IaC, Kubernetes.
SRE: Reliability metrics, incident response, automation.
Platform: Developer experience, service mesh, scalability.
AI/ML Ops: Model deployment, data pipelines, MLflow/Kubeflow.
💡 Tip: Create a Role-Skill Matrix to focus your learning.

✅ 2. Build Hands-On Projects
Deploy a 3-tier app on Kubernetes using Terraform + Helm.
Add observability dashboards with Prometheus & Grafana.
For AI/ML Ops: Deploy a ML model on GKE with CI/CD pipeline.
🔥 Pro Tip: Share screenshots or short videos of your projects on LinkedIn—it shows real skills!

✅ 3. Practice Scenario-Based Q&A
Interviewers love real-world problem-solving:
“How would you design a multi-region failover architecture?”
“Your CI/CD pipeline fails during artifact upload—how do you debug?”
“Latency spikes in production—what’s your approach?”
Use STAR (Situation, Task, Action, Result) for structured answers.

✅ 4. Reliability & Performance
Understand SLI/SLO/SLA, cost optimization, and incident drills.
💡 Insight: Share your learnings as bite-sized posts—great for engagement!

✅ 5. Mock Interviews & Feedback
Platforms like Pramp or Interviewing.io help you refine clarity and confidence.
